Makes "is-supported-script" accept a script that needs complex shaping, such as
Myanmar or Devanagari, where a font face of the style covers it. Native refused
those scripts outright, because glyph PBFs can't shape them, even though HarfBuzz
shapes the text that a style's font-faces draw. Styles such as Protomaps use the
expression to show a place's local name only where the renderer can draw it, so
native dropped those names. Symbol layout now passes the style's font faces to
the expression in a layer's filter and its text-field, and the parser no longer
folds the expression into a constant, as GL JS doesn't.
Issue: https://github.com/maplibre/maplibre-native/issues/4500
Upstream: not proposed

